From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:41:54 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/38] Lay out SwiftUI apps in iOS's safe area on Linux

The window's hosting controller now keeps SwiftUI's content clear of the
status bar and the home indicator, as on iOS, where it laid out from the
edges of the screen before.

As on iOS, scroll views reach under the bars and the home indicator along
the axes they scroll, with their content starting and ending clear of
them, and presentations cover the whole screen: their dimming, a sheet
down to the bottom edge with its content above the home indicator, and
menus, whose anchors are in the screen's coordinates.
---
